# The Zenodo concept DOI is added under `identifiers:` once the GitHub release mints it
# (see issue #138).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23428424"
    description: "Concept DOI (resolves to the latest version)"
title: "chromium-preprocessing: a Snakemake workflow for 10x Chromium single-cell preprocessing"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that pre-processes raw 10x Genomics Chromium single-cell
  data — gene expression, feature barcoding (CITE/HTO), and V(D)J — by running
  Cell Ranger (count / multi / aggr), restructuring and annotating the outputs,
  optionally pre-filtering cells for demultiplexing, and generating HTML QC
  reports. It runs standalone or as a git submodule within a DVC-tracked dataset.
